Subject: [PATCH 1/2] traj2control: heading from (right, forward), as the poses are ordered (upstream PR #57)

Upstream PR #57 (yuan-yin, open since 12 Nov 2025), verbatim. `traj2control`
builds the iLQR reference in (forward, right) but unpacks each waypoint as
(a, b) = (right, forward), so the heading is arctan2(d_forward, d_right): about
+90 deg for a straight plan, which the iLQR then steers to the right. Measured
on nuScenes scene-0013 with a straight constant-speed client: 4.3 m right in
14 m and into the kerb after 17 steps; with this change 0.00 m lateral drift.
The [-90, 90] deg wrap is kept as main has it.

`traj2control` is a module-level function that `closed_loop.py` imports by
name; no setting reaches it, so it has to be a patch. Without it part of every
model's lateral error is the controller's, not the model's.

Should go upstream (it is PR #57).

---
diff --git a/sim/utils/sim_utils.py b/sim/utils/sim_utils.py
index 8dd81d3..9a2b27a 100644
--- a/sim/utils/sim_utils.py
+++ b/sim/utils/sim_utils.py
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ def traj2control(plan_traj, info):
     plan_traj_stats = np.zeros((plan_traj.shape[0]+1, 5))
     plan_traj_stats[1:, :2] = plan_traj[:, [1,0]]
     prev_a, prev_b = 0.0, 0.0
-    for i, (a, b) in enumerate(plan_traj):
+    for i, (b, a) in enumerate(plan_traj):
         rot = np.arctan2(b - prev_b, a - prev_a)
         rot = np.where(rot > np.pi/2, rot - np.pi, rot)
         rot = np.where(rot < -np.pi/2, rot + np.pi, rot)
